1
00:00:09,700 --> 00:00:11,840
A gift box is a triangular prism.

2
00:00:11,890 --> 00:00:15,840
You want to know how much card is needed to make it.

3
00:00:15,890 --> 00:00:19,980
How many faces does it have, and what shapes are they?

4
00:00:20,030 --> 00:00:22,820
What are the faces of a triangular prism?

5
00:00:22,870 --> 00:00:26,080
Pause the video and choose.

6
00:00:26,130 --> 00:00:31,260
It has 2 triangles, one at each end, and 3 rectangles round the sides.

7
00:00:31,310 --> 00:00:32,990
That is 5 faces.

8
00:00:33,040 --> 00:00:37,080
Remember: a net is a flat shape that folds up to make a solid.

9
00:00:37,130 --> 00:00:38,940
It shows every face.

10
00:00:38,990 --> 00:00:42,780
The surface area is the total area of all the faces.

11
00:00:42,830 --> 00:00:49,260
Here is a prism whose ends are right-angled triangles with sides 3, 4 and 5 centimetres.

12
00:00:49,310 --> 00:00:51,730
It is 10 centimetres long.

13
00:00:51,780 --> 00:00:55,550
The three rectangles are 30, 40 and 50.

14
00:00:55,600 --> 00:01:01,390
Add everything: 12 plus 120 is 132 square centimetres.

15
00:01:01,440 --> 00:01:05,640
A pyramid has a base, and triangular faces that meet at a point.

16
00:01:05,690 --> 00:01:09,380
There is one triangle for each side of the base.

17
00:01:09,430 --> 00:01:16,970
For each triangle, use its slant height: the height of the triangle face, not the height of the pyramid.

18
00:01:17,020 --> 00:01:17,660
Your turn.

19
00:01:17,710 --> 00:01:20,980
How many faces does a square-based pyramid have?

20
00:01:21,030 --> 00:01:24,250
Pause the video and try it.

21
00:01:24,300 --> 00:01:28,520
1 square base, plus 4 triangles, makes 5 faces.

22
00:01:28,570 --> 00:01:29,860
Here is the method.

23
00:01:29,910 --> 00:01:33,360
Step 1: sketch the net, or list the faces.

24
00:01:33,410 --> 00:01:35,790
Step 2: find the area of each face.

25
00:01:35,840 --> 00:01:38,150
Triangles need a half b h.

26
00:01:38,200 --> 00:01:41,290
Step 3: group the identical faces.

27
00:01:41,340 --> 00:01:45,270
Step 4: add them all, and give the units squared.

28
00:01:45,320 --> 00:01:49,670
A square-based pyramid has a base of side 4 centimetres.

29
00:01:49,720 --> 00:01:52,660
Each triangle has a slant height of 6.

30
00:01:52,710 --> 00:01:55,410
The base is 4 times 4, which is 16.

31
00:01:55,460 --> 00:01:59,580
Each triangle is a half times 4 times 6, which is 12.

32
00:01:59,630 --> 00:02:01,700
4 triangles make 48.

33
00:02:01,750 --> 00:02:07,190
The total is 16 plus 48, which is 64 square centimetres.

34
00:02:07,240 --> 00:02:07,900
Your turn.

35
00:02:07,950 --> 00:02:12,000
A square base of side 6 has triangles with slant height 5.

36
00:02:12,050 --> 00:02:13,770
What is the surface area?

37
00:02:13,820 --> 00:02:16,730
Pause and work it out.

38
00:02:16,780 --> 00:02:18,140
The base is 36.

39
00:02:18,190 --> 00:02:23,120
Each triangle is a half times 6 times 5, which is 15.

40
00:02:23,170 --> 00:02:25,000
4 triangles make 60.

41
00:02:25,050 --> 00:02:27,150
36 plus 60 is 96.

42
00:02:27,200 --> 00:02:31,940
A tent has triangular ends with base 2 metres and height 1.5.

43
00:02:31,990 --> 00:02:35,230
Its two sloping sides are 1.8 by 3 metres.

44
00:02:35,280 --> 00:02:36,490
It has no floor.

45
00:02:36,540 --> 00:02:39,150
The two ends make 3 square metres.

46
00:02:39,200 --> 00:02:41,040
The two sides make 10.8.

47
00:02:41,090 --> 00:02:44,650
In total, 13.8 square metres of fabric.

48
00:02:44,700 --> 00:02:51,040
A prism has triangles of a half times 4 times 3, and rectangles of 40, 30 and 50.

49
00:02:51,090 --> 00:02:53,330
Raj adds up the surface area.

50
00:02:53,380 --> 00:02:55,460
Which line is wrong?

51
00:02:55,510 --> 00:02:56,570
Line 1 is wrong.

52
00:02:56,620 --> 00:02:59,830
There are two triangular ends, not one.

53
00:02:59,880 --> 00:03:04,400
2 times 6 is 12, plus 120 is 132.

54
00:03:04,450 --> 00:03:08,200
Some chocolate bars are sold in triangular prism boxes.

55
00:03:08,250 --> 00:03:13,790
Designers work out the surface area to know how much card each box needs.

56
00:03:13,840 --> 00:03:20,400
Saving even a few square centimetres per box adds up to a lot of card over millions of boxes.

57
00:03:20,450 --> 00:03:21,630
One last question.

58
00:03:21,680 --> 00:03:24,310
How many faces does a tetrahedron have?

59
00:03:24,360 --> 00:03:27,550
Pause the video and answer.

60
00:03:27,600 --> 00:03:29,450
A tetrahedron has 4 faces.

61
00:03:29,500 --> 00:03:31,680
They are all triangles.

62
00:03:31,730 --> 00:03:36,320
To remember: surface area is the total area of all the faces.

63
00:03:36,370 --> 00:03:40,840
A triangular prism has 2 triangles and 3 rectangles.

64
00:03:40,890 --> 00:03:43,310
A pyramid has a base plus triangles.

65
00:03:43,360 --> 00:03:45,370
Use the slant heights.

66
00:03:45,420 --> 00:03:48,150
A net helps you not to miss a face.

67
00:03:48,200 --> 00:03:53,550
Great work! Now practise lesson 15.4 on Camday.
